================================================================================
Third-party assets
================================================================================

roqsim's own code is Apache-2.0. The repository additionally VENDORS third-party robot descriptions,
meshes, textures, characters and scenes, each of which keeps its own license. Some of those licenses
(notably CC-BY-4.0) make ATTRIBUTION A CONDITION OF REDISTRIBUTION: if you redistribute this
repository, a package built from it, or the assets on their own, the corresponding notices must
travel with them.

The authoritative, per-asset records are:

  * a THIRD_PARTY.md in each package that keeps one, for provenance a one-line record is too
    short for
        roqsim_assets/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_humanoid/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_manipulation_assets/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_quadruped/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_scenes/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_walker/THIRD_PARTY.md
  * a CREDITS.txt in the folder of each prop, texture, scene, character and clip set (source,
    license, required attribution), e.g. roqsim_walker/src/roqsim_walker/models/people/<name>/
  * a license file beside each vendored robot, arm, gripper and sensor model, with its copyright
    notice where upstream gives one, e.g.
    roqsim_manipulation_assets/src/roqsim_manipulation_assets/models/ur10e/UR10e_LICENSE
    (in roqsim_aerial, roqsim_mobile, roqsim_mobile_manipulation, roqsim_manipulation_assets and
    roqsim_sensors under src/<package>/models/<name>/; in roqsim_humanoid and roqsim_quadruped
    under src/<package>/models/LICENSE.* and src/<package>/policy/LICENSE.*)

Each CREDITS.txt and license file ships in its package beside the files it covers. This file
summarises them by license and lists no asset; an asset's terms and attribution are in its own
record.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where the public/private line falls
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vendored robot descriptions under BSD / Apache-2.0 / MIT / MPL-2.0 are redistributable and
re-fetchable from public upstreams, so they are shipped here. Curated artwork whose upstream is
gated behind an account or an API token is not shipped, even when its license would allow it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The licenses of the bundled assets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BSD (3-Clause, 2-Clause, and BSD as an upstream package manifest declares it without a text)
    Robot, arm, gripper and sensor descriptions and meshes, and locomotion policies. Each model's
    license file carries the copyright notice and conditions the license requires to be retained.

Apache License 2.0
    Robot, arm, gripper and sensor descriptions and meshes, a locomotion policy, and a scene. Each
    model's license file, or the scene's CREDITS.txt, carries the license and its provenance. No
    vendored upstream ships a NOTICE file of its own.

MIT
    Robot, aerial vehicle and sensor descriptions and meshes. Each model's license file carries the
    copyright notice and permission notice the license requires.

Mozilla Public License 2.0  --  file-level copyleft; these notices must be retained
    A robot description and its meshes:
    roqsim_humanoid/src/roqsim_humanoid/models/LICENSE.genie_sim and roqsim_humanoid/THIRD_PARTY.md.

CC-BY 4.0  --  ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED ON REDISTRIBUTION
    Props, a scene, pedestrian characters and every locomotion clip. The attribution each requires
    is its folder's CREDITS.txt, which travels with the files, and its package's THIRD_PARTY.md.
    Every walker moves with the CC-BY clips, so anything shipping roqsim_walker's models/anims/, or
    a character driven by them, ships their attribution too (roqsim_walker/THIRD_PARTY.md).

CC0 1.0  --  no attribution required
    Surface textures, pedestrian characters and the parts a scene includes; their CREDITS.txt or
    THIRD_PARTY.md credits them all the same.

Vendor CAD under the vendor's own terms  --  NOT redistributed
    Some sensor meshes are converted from a vendor's published CAD. Those meshes are not committed:
    they are fetched and converted on demand (external/external_assets.yaml), and the license file
    beside each such model says where from.

NVIDIA asset license  --  NOT redistributed
    A locomotion policy under NVIDIA's asset license (local/internal R&D use only, not modifiable or
    redistributable) is not committed to this repository; it is downloaded on demand. See
    roqsim_quadruped/THIRD_PARTY.md.

roqsim's own work in the asset folders (Apache-2.0)
    Props and models authored for roqsim say so in their CREDITS.txt, license file or model file,
    and are covered by this repository's Apache-2.0 license.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
